#### 8\. Posing guide

Models make posing look so easy, but for most of us, knowing how to pose for photos is challenging.

This top lead magnet idea addresses this. [Savvy Leigh](https://savvyleigh.com/), a Charlotte wedding photographer, created a downloadable complete with her top five engagement poses—and you can do something similar. Your experience in guiding clients on how to stand, sit, smile, and interact naturally to produce great images is valuable knowledge— _for those in front and behind the camera._

Your lead magnet could be a resource that includes step-by-step instructions, illustrated by your photographs to cover a range of scenarios—from solo portraits to family shoots. The guide can include:

- Posing techniques
- Posing mistakes to avoid
- Tips to convey emotion
- Outdoor vs indoor posing
- Creative posing

The list goes on. By offering all of this information, you’re sure to put your audience at ease and win their business.

#### 9\. Photo editing basics

Capturing stunning images is just one part of the photography journey. Editing transforms good photos into exceptional ones. In a nod to the many enthusiasts who delve into photo editing only to realize its complexities, you can design a strategic lead magnet to both educate and convert.

Why not craft a downloadable guide that outlines essential photo editing techniques and emphasizes the value of professional editing services? Touch on foundational editing concepts, such as color correction, exposure adjustments, and composition enhancements. Be sure to showcase real examples of images that you’ve touched up.

Alternatively, create step-by-step tutorials on how to use popular editing software. Throughout your guide, subtly emphasize the benefits of having a professional work on images, drawing attention to the nuances that can be challenging for amateurs to master.

### Discounts & freebies

Providing a discount code in exchange for an opt-in is a tried-and-tested way to generate leads for photographers. It provides great motivation to click the subscribe button and really goes the extra mile to sway a potential client who’s debating making a booking.

The following photographers came up with innovative lead magnets that provide their audience with some kind of discount or freebie.

#### 10\. First session discount

[Jamiya Wilson](https://www.jwheadshots.com/) of JW Headshots is a New York-based photographer who’s an expert in actor and corporate headshots. He loves creating images that show his clients’ diverse personalities and help them stand out from the crowd.

Let’s face it: great headshots don’t come cheap. Although they’re a worthy investment, they’re an investment nevertheless. That’s why Jamiya’s lead magnet makes such a big difference. When someone subscribes to his email list, he sends a coupon for $25 off their first session if they book within 30 days.

This lead magnet shows great marketing prowess because it gives people the opportunity to save some money, but there’s a time limit involved. Instead of hemming and hawing, they’ll be motivated to make their decision quickly and get great headshots at a discounted price.

#### 11\. Free phone wallpapers

[Paul Nicklen](https://paulnicklen.com/) is one of the most well-regarded wildlife photographers out there. He’s based in Canada but travels far and wide to capture powerful images of creatures in their natural habitats. Without knowing it, you’ve probably seen one of Paul’s images before.

Paul uses a unique lead magnet that appeals to different audiences. When you subscribe to Paul’s email list, you receive five phone wallpapers of some of his favorite animal encounters for free.

This is a great lead magnet idea because it’s genuinely useful _(who doesn’t need a new phone background?)_ and shows off Paul’s skills as a wildlife photographer. He also uses images that he’s already taken, so there was no need to shoot something new for his lead magnet.

If you specialize in wildlife or landscape photography, giving away images as phone backgrounds is an excellent lead magnet idea.

#### 12\. Free extra images

[The Boudoir Divas](https://www.boudoirphotographysandiego.com/the-boudoir-divas-studio39305610) are an all-woman photography team based out of San Diego. They’ve been working in the industry for 15 years and specialize in everything boudoir. They love creating unique photoshoot experiences and helping women celebrate themselves.

The Boudoir Divas use an effective popup lead magnet on their photography website. Once you’ve spent a few seconds browsing, their form appears. If you sign up for their mailing list, you can get two digital images for free (an $80 value) when you do a photoshoot with them.

Getting these extra freebies is an enticing treat for clients. After a successful photoshoot, it can be difficult to narrow down their image selections to fit the package they purchased. This lead magnet offers a couple of bonus images to enjoy for years to come.

