### Miscellaneous

Some download ideas to drive lead generation for photographers don’t fit into any specific category, like the photographer below who uses a unique, interactive [quiz lead magnet](https://flodesk.com/blog/why-your-business-needs-a-quiz-and-how-to-make-one/) on her website.

#### 13\. Creative superpower quiz results

[KT Merry](https://ktmerryeducation.com/) is a luxury destination and editorial photographer. She’s worked everywhere from beaches in the Maldives to the Serengeti National Park and has been featured in _Vogue_, _People_, _Elle_, and more.

We’re big fans of the lead magnet KT Merry uses on her website. Rather than relying on more typical downloads, she’s put together a quiz entitled _“What is your creative superpower?”_

It provides interesting information to photographers, is on-brand for KT Merry, and certainly isn’t something you see every day.

All a reader has to do is choose their answers and opt-in to her email list. Then, they’ll receive an immediate message with their results and can put these insights into action for their photography businesses.

#### 14\. Filter presets

It’s the age of Instagram—filters are “in.” And you have a unique opportunity to create one-of-a-kind filter presets and place them behind the paywall of your newsletter signup. Offering presets provides tangible benefits for new or busy photographers while giving you a direct line of communication for ongoing engagement and potential conversion.

The best place to start when creating filter presets is to consider your unique photography style and aesthetic. In the example above, [Hope Taylor](https://hopetaylor.com/) provides presents that capture her signature light, bright, and bold style.

When marketing your presets, position your messaging around their exclusivity and the value they bring to subscribers—like the one-click implementation promised in this example.

## The elements of an excellent lead magnet

We hope that the photography lead magnets we’ve curated have motivated and inspired you to build your own.

Of course, there are myriad ways to go about developing a great lead magnet. But there are a few key elements you should always keep in mind for great results.

### Solve a problem

If you’re not sure where to start with your photography lead magnet, make a list of the kind of photography-related problems your ideal client or target audience might face. They could be anything from _“I don’t know how to pose naturally for photos,”_ to _“I don’t know what to wear to get a headshot taken.”_

Once you’ve established your clients’ biggest problems, make a lead magnet that provides them with a solution. Your audience is most likely to convert if they see a resource that can help them directly.

### Keep good design practices in mind

Remember, your lead magnet represents your photography services. It’s an extension of your brand, so you’ve got to make sure it looks fantastic. Keep good design practices in mind, choose high quality images, and make sure everything looks professional.

As a photographer, you’re in the business of making things look beautiful! You’ll never attract clients if your lead magnet doesn’t live up to those same standards.

### Show off your skills

There are _so many_ talented photographers out there. The best way to differentiate yourself from the crowd is by showing off your unique abilities, skills, and styles.

A photography lead magnet is a great opportunity to demonstrate the skills that make you special. It gives you a space to put your expertise on display, whether that means sharing your custom presets or your favorite night-time photography tips.

### Make it simple

When building your lead magnet, don’t make things too complicated. In all likelihood, this will be your audience’s first major connection with you and your business. If you send them a resource that’s overly long, technical, or complicated, then they might get overwhelmed and lose interest.

Your first lead magnet should be something simple and valuable that your audience can digest easily.

**_Quick tip:_** _Once you’ve landed a new subscriber, don’t forget to send_ [_lead nurturing emails_](https://flodesk.com/blog/lead-nurturing-email-examples/) _to keep them engaged!_

